! mcp_bootstrap_p98.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 98:
! THE CONVERSION SUBROUTINE, AND THE END OF THE ASSEMBLY.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.105, header "PAGE NUMBER 98" --
! read, not assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11C11IPL  CARD ID 18000787  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 98".
!
! THIRTY-SEVEN LINES, AND THE COUNT IS MEASURED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! right-hand LOCATION column prints the card serial of every line:
! 18000787 on line 1 down to 18000823 on line 37, thirty-seven
! consecutive serials with no break, so line N = serial - 18000786.
! Twenty-nine of those lines produce something the oracle can check:
! nineteen compile a word or half-word (!CHECK) and ten are SYN
! cards whose printed location is the check (!SYM, plus the four
! on-page labels).  Eight compile nothing -- 1-4, 21, 22, 35, 37.
!
! >>> THIS IS THE LAST PAGE OF THE ASSEMBLY. <<<  Line 37 is
! "UNTAIL,(2)" and nothing follows it.  Lines 22-36 are a block the
! listing itself labels "ADDITIONS MADE TO MAKE ASSIGNMT. COMPATIBLE"
! -- SYN declarations of names the ASSIGN program owns, carried here
! so the two assemble together.  They cost no storage; their printed
! LOCATION carries the "+" suffix that marks a definition.
!
! NOT CONTIGUOUS WITH THE LAST TRANSCRIBED PAGE.  printed p.96 ends
! at 005424.00 (a half-word, so storage ends 005424.40) and this page
! begins at 005450.40.  printed p.97 is not transcribed and holds the
! 0o24 words in between.  Nothing here depends on p.97.
!
! >>> WHAT THE ROUTINE DOES. <<<  T MCONV expands a 48-bit, 6-bit-byte
! field at $R+.16 into 8-bit bytes (line 6), contracts it to 4-bit
! bytes at $R+.32 (line 7), and then walks the 4-bit bytes from the
! right with LXA: line 10 asks whether the byte is 1010, line 12
! replaces it by 0000 if it is, line 13 asks whether the NEXT byte is
! 0000 and line 14 loops back while it is.  Line 15 turns the final
! index into a field length, line 16 fetches it as a 6-bit byte from
! LXA+.18, line 17 loads it into $L, line 18 does the convert proper
! (LCV from $R+.32 under $L) and line 19 returns through T MX1.  The
! comments on the page say exactly this: "-EXPAND TO 8 BIT BYTES.",
! "-CONTRACT TO 4-BIT BYTES.", "-IS 4-BIT BYTE 1010.", "- NO----
! BRANCH", "- YES --- REPLACE BY 0000.", "-IS NEXT BYTE 0000.",
! "- NO----GO BACK.", "-COMPUTE FIELD LENGTH.", "-CONVERT.",
! "-OUT OF ROUTINE."
!
! >>> THE DRUM OPENS EVERY ROUND GLYPH ON THIS PAGE. <<<  The page's
! own column headings print "LCCATICN" for LOCATION and the boxed
! title prints "CCNVERSICN SUBRCUTINE", so a round glyph here is as
! likely to be O or 0 as C.  Three readings settled the hex bytes,
! and none of them was "look harder":
!
!   (1) THE OCTAL FIELDS IN THE SAME ROW.  Line 5's location prints
!       "0C545C.4C" -- the first two fields are octal and cannot hold
!       a C, so this row drops ink on three zeros before it reaches
!       its hex byte, and the byte is 00, not CC.
!   (2) THE INDEX NIBBLE.  The low nibble of the trailing byte is the
!       index register of the indexed operand.  LXA is $12 = 0xC, so
!       lines 10, 12 and 13 -- .4(LXA), -.4(LXA), 0.0(LXA) -- print a
!       GENUINE C in "8C", and line 18's second half-word ends "3C"
!       because its second operand is 0.0(LXA).  Line 19's B,0.0(T
!       MX1) with T MX1 = $1 ends "01" and line 23's unindexed BD,$
!       ends "00".  These C's are structure, not ink.
!   (3) THE ASSEMBLER.  Every one of the nineteen rows below was
!       assembled before it was believed, and all nineteen
!       reproduce the printed binary bit for bit on the first
!       run, as do all seventeen symbol locations.
!
! >>> FOUR SPELLINGS WERE DECIDED BY AN INDEPENDENT PAGE, NOT BY EYE.
! The listing_oracle checks locations and binary and never checks a
! label's spelling, so each round glyph in a NAME was settled against
! a page transcribed separately:
!   line  9  LBLZOR  -- printed "LBLZCR".  printed p.54 line 81 has
!            LBLZOR SYN(BU,8,8),(8)2601.63 and this row's first
!            half-word is 002601.63 80, the same bit to the bit.
!   lines 28/29  YLOL2 / YLOL1 -- printed "YLCL2"/"YLCL1".  printed
!            p.39 has YLOL2 (8)5464.40 and YLOL1 (8)5465.0, which are
!            exactly the two locations printed here.
!   line 30  SYSMOD -- printed "SYSMCD"; the comment beside it reads
!            "-TWO BIT OPERATING MODE".
!   line 34  SCORG  -- printed "SCCRG".  printed p.39 line 19 already
!            has SCORG at (8)2151.03, this page's location.
! Also checked against other decks and matching exactly: STATI 0.26,
! SIMNT 0.53 and SMOUNT 0.51 (printed pp.69/70), Y BCRD (8)5464.0
! (p.39), S MAXUB (8)2153.0 (p.40), X IN END (8)5466.0 (pp.13/15/17).
!
! >>> ONE GLYPH I COULD NOT DECIDE AND DID NOT PRETEND TO. <<<  Line
! 23's name prints "Y B?RD", the fourth character an open round glyph
! identical to the O of "ADDITIONS" two lines above and to the C of
! "CNOP" one line above -- this drum prints BOTH that way.  It is
! spelled YBCRD here because printed p.39's landed deck spells it
! YBCRD and the merge has to agree with itself; the binary does not
! depend on it.  Line 27's "D FREE" IS decidable: its first glyph has
! the straight vertical left stem and squared corners of the D in
! "BCRD" and of "SYSMCD"'s last letter, which the round C of "CNOP"
! does not have.
!
! >>> TWO SPELLINGS strap_asm WOULD NOT TAKE, AND ONE IT WOULD. <<<
!   line 12 prints "$CMC000(BU,4,4),-.4(LXA)".  strap_asm rejects the
!     "$" prefix with KeyError '$CM0000'; written CM0000 it assembles
!     to the printed word exactly.  The printed spelling is kept
!     verbatim in the !CHECK note.
!   line 37's "UNTAIL,(2)" IS accepted verbatim, and so is line 10's
!     "KF(BU,4,4)(V+I)" with the modifier AFTER the mode -- printed
!     p.88 puts it before, and strap_asm takes either.
!
! >>> A BIT OFFSET UNDER "(8)" IS OCTAL, FRACTION INCLUDED. <<<  The
! origin here is written SLC,(8)5450.40, NOT (8)5450.32: strap_asm
! parses the fraction of an (8) literal in base 8, so (8)5450.32 is
! bit 26 and lands six bits low.  It happens to still produce the
! right address for line 5 -- a half-word instruction realigns -- so
! this one is invisible to the oracle and is written down instead.
! The STATEMENT column is the other way round: its offsets are
! DECIMAL, which is why line 24's ",.26" prints as location
! 000000.32, line 30's "SCOMRG+.8" as 002151.10, and line 16's
! "LXA+.18" as 000034.22.
!
! >>> ONE OPERAND I READ BUT DID NOT CONFIRM. <<<  Line 18's mode
! field prints "(DU,C,4)" and I read the middle character as 0, a
! round open glyph like every other 0 on the page.  The row
! assembles bit-identically with it, so the bits are right; what I
! have NOT done is check against a primary source what a zero
! LENGTH in a DU mode field means.  Line 17 loads $L immediately
! before, which is consistent with the length coming from $L at
! execution, but that is a reading of the code and not a citation.
!
! >>> THE STATEMENT OPERANDS ARE WRITTEN AS THE PAGE PRINTS THEM.
! Lines 24-26 are ",.26" / ",.53" / ",.51" with no leading zero,
! which is what the page prints; other decks write "0.26".  Both
! assemble to the same bit and the printed form was chosen on
! purpose.
!
! >>> TWO LISTING MARKS: lines 6 and 29 carry an asterisk after the
! location (005451.00 * and 005465.00 *).
!
! Five symbols are carried as SYN stand-ins from pages transcribed
! elsewhere.  Only T MLXA's value is NOT confirmed by a row on this
! page: lines 8/10/12/13/15/16/18 all depend on LXA = T MLXA = $12,
! and they do reproduce the printed binary, so the page agrees with
! p.83 -- but p.83 is where the $12 came from.

TMLXA   SYN, $12                     ! p.83 line 33 -CONVERSION ROUTINE
TMX1    SYN, $1                      ! p.83 line 21
LBLZOR  SYN(BU,8,8), (8)2601.63      ! p.54 line 81
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)2151.0               ! p.33 (p.37 line 11 is the
                                      !   XW that allocates it)
SBAMCP  SYN, (8)2153.0               ! p.33 and p.72 (p.37 line 17
                                      !   is the VF that allocates it)

        SLC, (8)5450.40

! ---- THE CONVERSION SUBROUTINE ------------------------------------
TMCONV  NOP                          ! line 5
        LF(BU,48,6), $R+.16          ! line 6  -EXPAND TO 8 BIT BYTES.
        SF(BU,32,4), $R+.32          ! line 7  -CONTRACT TO 4-BIT BYTES.
        LVI, LXA, $R+.32             ! line 8
        LF(BU,8,8), LBLZOR, 32       ! line 9
LCONVA  KF(BU,4,4)(V+I), .4(LXA), 32 ! line 10 -IS 4-BIT BYTE 1010.
        BAH, LCONVB                  ! line 11 -   NO----BRANCH
        CM0000(BU,4,4), -.4(LXA)     ! line 12 -YES --- REPLACE BY 0000.
LCONVB  KF(BU,4,4), 0.0(LXA), 36     ! line 13 -IS NEXT BYTE 0000.
        BZAEZ, LCONVA                ! line 14 -   NO----GO BACK.
        V-I, LXA, $R+.32             ! line 15 -COMPUTE FIELD LENGTH.
        LF(BU,6,6), LXA+.18, 119     ! line 16
        LV, LXA, $L                  ! line 17
        LCV(DU,0,4), $R+.32, 0.0(LXA) ! line 18 -CONVERT.
        B, 0.0(TMX1)                 ! line 19 -OUT OF ROUTINE.
LXA     SYN, TMLXA                   ! line 20
        CNOP                         ! line 21

! ---- ADDITIONS MADE TO MAKE ASSIGNMT. COMPATIBLE ------------------
YBCRD   BD, $                        ! line 23 -UNCODE PATH NOT TO BE TAKEN
STATI   SYN(BU,1), .26               ! line 24
SIMNT   SYN(BU,1), .53               ! line 25
SMOUNT  SYN(BU,1), .51               ! line 26
DFREE   SYN, 0                       ! line 27
YLOL2   VF                           ! line 28
YLOL1   VF                           ! line 29
SYSMOD  SYN(BU,2), SCOMRG+.8         ! line 30 -TWO BIT OPERATING MODE
STERMI  VF, ZFINIS                   ! line 31 -THE LAST LOC USED BY MCP
ZFINIS  SYN, (8)17777.0              ! line 32
SMAXUB  SYN, SBAMCP                  ! line 33 -MAX UB+1 THAT CAN BE USED
SCORG   SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.3         ! line 34 -TH+ COMPILE GO BITS
        CNOP                         ! line 35
XINEND  SYN, $                       ! line 36
        UNTAIL, (2)                  ! line 37

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- all thirty-seven lines.  Lines 1-4, 21, 22
! and 35-37 print no LOCATION and no BINARY OUTPUT.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1                                             *-------------------
!   line  2                                             - CONVERSION SUBROUTINE
!   line  3                                             *-------------------
!   line  4                                             -
!   line  5  005450.40   000000.30 00                   T MCONV NOP
!   line  6  005451.00 * 000011.20 80  060600.06 70             LF(BU,48,6),$R+.16
!   line  7  005452.00   000011.40 80  040400.12 F0             SF(BU,32,4),$R+.32
!   line  8  005453.00   000011.71 01                           LVI,LXA,$R+.32
!   line  9  005453.40   002601.63 80  010020.06 70             LF(BU,8,8),LBLZOR,32
!   line 10  005454.40   000000.04 8C  104420.23 10   L CONVA   KF(BU,4,4)(V+I),.4(LXA),32
!   line 11  005455.40   005457.37 42                           BAH,LCONVB
!   line 12  005456.00   777777.74 8C  004400.00 F0             $CM0000(BU,4,4),-.4(LXA)
!   line 13  005457.00   000000.00 8C  004422.23 10   L CONVB   KF(BU,4,4),0.0(LXA),36
!   line 14  005460.00   005454.76 C4                           BZAEZ,LCONVA
!   line 15  005460.40   000011.71 0D                           V-I,LXA,$R+.32
!   line 16  005461.00   000034.22 80  006673.46 70             LF(BU,6,6),LXA+.18,119
!   line 17  005462.00   000010.30 30                           LV,LXA,$L
!   line 18  005462.40   000011.40 80  000400.24 3C             LCV(DU,0,4),$R+.32,0.0(LXA)
!   line 19  005463.40   000000.10 01                           B,0.0(T MX1)
!   line 20  000034.00+  +00000000     BU,100,10     L XA       SYN,TMLXA
!   line 21                                                     CNOP
!   line 22                                             - ADDITIONS MADE TO MAKE ASSIGNMT. COMPATIBLE
!   line 23  005464.00   005464.04 00                 Y BCRD    BD,$
!   line 24  000000.32+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10     STATI      SYN(BU,1),.26
!   line 25  000000.65+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10     SIMNT      SYN(BU,1),.53
!   line 26  000000.63+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10     S MOUNT    SYN(BU,1),.51
!   line 27  000000.00+  +00000000     NULL          D FREE     SYN,0
!   line 28  005464.40   000000.00+                  YLOL2      VF
!   line 29  005465.00 * 000000.00+                  YLOL1      VF
!   line 30  002151.10+  +00000000     BU,02 ,10     SYSMOD     SYN(BU,2),SCOMRG+.8
!   line 31  005465.40   017777.00+                  S TERMI    VF,ZFINIS
!   line 32  017777.00+  +00000000     NULL          Z FINIS    SYN,(8)17777.0
!   line 33  002153.00+  +00000000     B ,31 ,01     S MAXUB    SYN,S BA MCP
!   line 34  002151.03+  +00000000     BU,01 ,10     SCORG      SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.3
!   line 35                                                     CNOP
!   line 36  005466.00+  +00000000     NULL          X IN END   SYN,$
!   line 37                                                     UNTAIL,(2)

! WHICH ROWS ARE INDEPENDENT CHECKS.
!   SELF-CONTAINED, resting on nothing outside this page: lines 5, 7,
!   11, 14, 17, 23, 28, 29 and 31.  Lines 11 and 14 branch to LCONVB
!   and LCONVA, both defined by rows on this page (005457.00 and
!   005454.40), so they really do close on themselves.
!   REST ON $R, $L (C22-6531 Appendix A, words 9 and 8): lines 6, 7,
!   8, 15, 17, 18.  Those are the assembler's own register table, not
!   another transcription.
!   REST ON AN EXTERNAL SYN: line 9 on LBLZOR (p.54), line 19 on
!   T MX1 (p.83), lines 8/10/12/13/15/16/18 and !SYM LXA on T MLXA
!   (p.83), !SYM SYSMOD and !SYM SCORG on SCOMRG (p.33), !SYM SMAXUB
!   on SBAMCP (p.33/p.72).  Each of those external addresses is
!   CONFIRMED here rather than assumed: the page prints the location
!   or the binary that the external value produces, and they agree.

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 98 -----------------
!SYM   TMCONV   005450.40
!SYM   LCONVA   005454.40
!SYM   LCONVB   005457.00
!SYM   LXA      000034.00
!SYM   YBCRD    005464.00
!SYM   STATI    000000.32
!SYM   SIMNT    000000.65
!SYM   SMOUNT   000000.63
!SYM   DFREE    000000.00
!SYM   YLOL2    005464.40
!SYM   YLOL1    005465.00
!SYM   SYSMOD   002151.10
!SYM   STERMI   005465.40
!SYM   ZFINIS   017777.00
!SYM   SMAXUB   002153.00
!SYM   SCORG    002151.03
!SYM   XINEND   005466.00
!CHECK 005450.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 5  T MCONV NOP
!CHECK 005451.00 | 000011.20 80 060600.06 70 | line 6  LF(BU,48,6),$R+.16
!CHECK 005452.00 | 000011.40 80 040400.12 F0 | line 7  SF(BU,32,4),$R+.32
!CHECK 005453.00 | 000011.71 01 | line 8  LVI,LXA,$R+.32
!CHECK 005453.40 | 002601.63 80 010020.06 70 | line 9  LF(BU,8,8),LBLZOR,32
!CHECK 005454.40 | 000000.04 8C 104420.23 10 | line 10 L CONVA KF(BU,4,4)(V+I),.4(LXA),32
!CHECK 005455.40 | 005457.37 42 | line 11 BAH,LCONVB
!CHECK 005456.00 | 777777.74 8C 004400.00 F0 | line 12 printed "$CM0000(BU,4,4),-.4(LXA)"
!CHECK 005457.00 | 000000.00 8C 004422.23 10 | line 13 L CONVB KF(BU,4,4),0.0(LXA),36
!CHECK 005460.00 | 005454.76 C4 | line 14 BZAEZ,LCONVA
!CHECK 005460.40 | 000011.71 0D | line 15 V-I,LXA,$R+.32
!CHECK 005461.00 | 000034.22 80 006673.46 70 | line 16 LF(BU,6,6),LXA+.18,119
!CHECK 005462.00 | 000010.30 30 | line 17 LV,LXA,$L
!CHECK 005462.40 | 000011.40 80 000400.24 3C | line 18 LCV(DU,0,4),$R+.32,0.0(LXA)
!CHECK 005463.40 | 000000.10 01 | line 19 B,0.0(T MX1)
!CHECK 005464.00 | 005464.04 00 | line 23 Y BCRD BD,$
!CHECK 005464.40 | 000000.00+ | line 28 YLOL2 VF
!CHECK 005465.00 | 000000.00+ | line 29 YLOL1 VF
!CHECK 005465.40 | 017777.00+ | line 31 S TERMI VF,ZFINIS
